    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Let's say I have a tag like this : `<span style=\"some styles...\">some content</span>`. If I replace the `span` with a `p` using mini.surround, the whole tag with it's `style` attribute is replaced and I end up with `<p>some content</p>`. \r\n\r\nIs there a way to keep the tag attributes and have something like `<p style=\"some styles...\">some content</p>` at the end?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Let's say I have a tag like this : <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;span style=\"some styles...\"&gt;some content&lt;/span&gt;</code>. If I replace the <code class=\"notranslate\">span</code> with a <code class=\"notranslate\">p</code> using mini.surround, the whole tag with it's <code class=\"notranslate\">style</code> attribute is replaced and I end up with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;p&gt;some content&lt;/p&gt;</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to keep the tag attributes and have something like <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;p style=\"some styles...\"&gt;some content&lt;/p&gt;</code> at the end?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Let's say I have a tag like this : <span style=\"some styles...\">some content</span>. If I replace the span with a p using mini.surround, the whole tag with it's style attribute is replaced and I end up with <p>some content</p>.\nIs there a way to keep the tag attributes and have something like <p style=\"some styles...\">some content</p> at the end?",
